  identity. It's out because JavaScript can't read an HttpOnly cookie, so the ID could not be a parameter to [38;5;153mlogin[39m or
  readable by other forms — it contradicts two things you've already decided. Worth knowing the tradeoff exists: we're
  choosing browser-readable storage deliberately, and it's defensible precisely because you made the ID
  non-authoritative.

